/* Board comps — real data only.
 *
 * GENERATED by tools/comps/scenarios.js from tools/fixtures/. Do not hand-edit:
 * regenerate instead, so a comp can never drift from the product’s own data.
 * Every clock time is read out of a captured fixture and converted UTC -> AEST
 * (+10). Minute arithmetic is web/js/time.js’s: both sides floored to the clock
 * minute, so a figure always agrees with the clock times printed beside it.
 *
 * THE DELTAS APPLIED, and there are no others. The fixtures were captured on
 * days with no disruption (estimated === planned on every leg), so a delayed or
 * cancelled board cannot be shown without one. Name every one of these in the
 * sheet’s lede, or the owner rules on a fixture artifact by mistake.
 *   `delayed`: the 09:24 runs 6 min late, the 09:54 runs 2 min late.
 *   `cancelled`: the 09:24 is cancelled.
 *   `tight`: the 09:24's FIRST leg runs 5 min late into Town Hall, so it
 *       arrives 09:56 instead of 09:51 and the printed 7-minute
 *       change becomes a 2-minute one. The connecting 09:58 is
 *       unchanged, so the trip still arrives 10:08. This is the only
 *       way to show a connection at risk from fixtures captured on
 *       undisrupted days, and it is a delta on a real journey.
 *
 * SOURCE trip_rhodes_bondijunction.json — 11 journeys; the five routed via the
 *   "On Demand - Inner West" bus (upstream product class 10) are excluded
 *   server-side per docs/contracts/api.md, so a client sees six. Two of the six
 *   return isRealtimeControlled: null on the first leg => SCHEDULED.
 * SOURCE trip_central_parramatta.json — 6 journeys, all single-leg. Carries the
 *   longest real headsign in the repo ("Mount Victoria via Parramatta") and the
 *   only two-digit platforms (7/8/12/13).
 * SOURCE trip_tallawong_chatswood.json — the metro saved trip’s identity.
 *
 * Classic script under file:// — every name below is a deliberate global.
 */

